WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 12 Leader Video
Unit 3, Lesson 4: Designer

1
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.340
So we've almost made it through science.

2
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.940
Now we've discovered that science is really a foundation

3
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.100
for understanding our world

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.860
and it does not contradict our faith.

5
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.340
Well, that's good news.

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.300
We've also taken a look at three really good pieces

7
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.980
of evidence that help us see that God is actually there,

8
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.900
that we have evidence for God.

9
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.060
We looked at the idea of fine-tuning.

10
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.220
We looked at the idea of DNA

11
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.940
and we looked at the idea of design.

12
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.340
All of these pointing to God in some way, shape, or form

13
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.580
through the use of science.

14
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.140
Now, I want you to keep in mind

15
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.620
two kinds of students this week.

16
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.620
The first kind is the student that has all this information

17
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.220
and is super fired up

18
00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.020
and ready to go with the best arguments

19
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.660
that they have to their teacher

20
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.300
who probably knows more than they do

21
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.220
about all these things,

22
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.340
especially this week with the idea of design

23
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.860
because this is where the conversation

24
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.740
between creation and evolution starts to really come alive.

25
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.740
And it might seem like this is a good idea

26
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.100
for them to jump off and start all these arguments

27
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.060
and try to win people to Christ

28
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.340
and they might try it and you want to champion that

29
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.940
but at the same time make sure that they do so

30
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.540
in truth and love.

31
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.460
That if they're gonna have these conversations

32
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.300
you don't want to tell them not to

33
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.460
and it's okay that they can challenge their teachers

34
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.220
and it's okay to challenge their students

35
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.500
but to do so with love

36
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.740
and to do so with the appropriate amount of respect

37
00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.220
especially for teachers

38
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:47.660
as well as engaging in the right kinds of conversations.

39
00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.340
Now, the other type of student

40
00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.500
is maybe the one that really is still not sure

41
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.060
or the one that wasn't sure

42
00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.940
before entering into this conversation.

43
00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.620
Now would be a really good time

44
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.180
to just take a step back and take inventory

45
00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.060
with that student and ask them the plain question.

46
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.460
Was this enough evidence?

47
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.860
Do you need more?

48
00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.900
What further questions do you have?

49
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.220
What clarifications do you need?

50
00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.340
Now remember the reason why we're doing this study.

51
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.620
It's so that our students can have a deep conviction

52
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.540
for themselves about what they believe

53
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.700
and why they believe it.

54
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.780
And to also be able to communicate that

55
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.060
in love and humility and do so relationally.

56
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.740
So while it might be really exciting

57
00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:33.500
to have some eager students to get started

58
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.340
and to get engaged in conversation,

59
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.100
help them be patient

60
00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.100
because there is so much more to learn.

